# export-ignore controls what `git archive` leaves out of the tree it
# packs. GoReleaser's `source:` block runs `git archive` under the hood
# (.goreleaser.yaml), so these entries are the actual filter for the
# release source tarball — not the archive block's own file globs, which
# have no negation syntax and cannot exclude anything.
# WARNING (v0.2 final review wave, 2026-08-20): vendor/ is safe to
# export-ignore ONLY because every current go.mod dependency
# (github.com/stretchr/testify, its go.yaml.in/yaml/v3 indirect) is a
# TEST-only dependency, imported solely by *_test.go files — which are
# themselves export-ignored below, so the released tarball never contains
# code that imports them and never needs vendor/ to build. go.mod itself
# is NOT export-ignored and ships in every release tarball as-is. The
# moment any non-test .go file (production code, not *_test.go) imports a
# third-party package, this line MUST be removed: otherwise the tarball
# ships a go.mod requiring a module its own vendor/ was stripped out of,
# and the extracted source cannot build standalone.
vendor/ export-ignore
integration/ export-ignore
tools/ export-ignore
docs/ export-ignore
examples/ export-ignore
testdata/ export-ignore
.superpowers/ export-ignore
.github/ export-ignore
*_test.go export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
# webui/ is the Vue admin panel's SOURCE (Vite/npm project) — CI and a
# release build never need node: admin_assets_gen.go (repo root, `make
# admin-ui`'s committed output) is the only artifact the plugin build
# actually depends on, exactly like vendor/ above is safe to drop because
# nothing at the repo root imports it directly.
webui/ export-ignore
